loads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/deployments","created_at":"2017-10-05T21:56:00Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T01:01:53Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-13T05:03:31Z","git_url":"git://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:yugabyte/yugabyte-db.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db","homepage":"https://www.yugabyte.com","size":908218,"stargazers_count":9958,"watchers_count":9958,"language":"C","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1201,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":7608,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","cpp","database","distributed-database","distributed-sql","distributed-sql-database","high-performance","kubernetes","multi-cloud","multi-region","scale-out","sql"],"visibility":"public","forks":1201,"open_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Long-running Jepsen append tests (~1200 seconds) of YugaByte DB 1.3.1.0 have seen repeated tserver crashes, due to both file limits and memory exhaustion. There are no forced crashes, partitions, or other nemesis activities in this test: it's just a healthy happy cluster trying to serve transactions. I've attached memory, rpc, and thread stats from the admin interface for the first node in one such test, while it was allocating ~5MB/sec of memory, but before it'd crashed.\r\n\r\n[Full Jepsen & node logs (16GB uncompressed)](http://jepsen.io.s3.amazonaws.com/analyses/yugabyte-db-1.3.1/20190815T190015.000Z.zip)\r\n[stats.tar.gz](https://github.com/YugaByte/yugabyte-db/files/3506907/stats.tar.gz)\r\n\r\nThe workload in question is a variant of the append test, where our reads perform a select on an un-indexed secondary key field (`k2`), rather than selecting by primary key.  Updates still use primary keys, in this particular test. You can reproduce this issue using Jepsen 0f46d2ea72b437a7c851bdce71757feaf2a2092f, and running (e.g. on EC2):\r\n\r\n```\r\nlein run test-all --username admin --nodes-file ~/nodes --os debian -w ysql/append --concurrency 3n --time-limit 1200 --test-count 10\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/2075/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/2075/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]